    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-001","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":3998479188,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"The new AI E2E delivery validator depended on a case-sensitive free-form substring that did not exactly match the canonical roadmap heading, so the governance gate rejected its own accepted document despite the intended concept being present.","horizontal_audit":["roadmap gate heading identifiers","validator-to-document vocabulary bindings","G2 Monitoring source onboarding","G7 Alert policy lifecycle","G14 Production release gate","future governance validators that bind prose to executable checks"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":11},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-002","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":3998814015,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"The credited delivery falsifier only asserted source substrings and then invoked an unrelated D4-C negative helper. It did not mutate delivery authority or execute the delivery validator, so learning credit could survive even if the actual delivery guard stopped enforcing the roadmap.","horizontal_audit":["credited falsifier semantic relevance","delivery-validator negative mutation","roadmap heading removal","workflow scheduling for credited probes","future cross-domain assurance probes"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":12},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-003","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":3998814018,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"The E2E-16 validator required only eight named layers plus a total length of sixteen. The remaining required layers could be replaced with arbitrary strings while preserving length.","horizontal_audit":["complete E2E-16 layer identity","ordered layer contract","duplicate layer detection","manifest schema drift","future Definition-of-Done revisions"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":13},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-004","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":3998814021,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"Gate dependency validation rejected only forward references and therefore accepted empty dependency lists, allowing the G0-to-G14 chain to disappear.","horizontal_audit":["gate predecessor relationships","sequential product execution ordering","dependency removal","parallelization safety","future roadmap graph evolution"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":14},
