    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-010","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4000314574,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"The strict learning checker registered only the generic must_fail helper, so an unrelated D4 negative call could statically credit the delivery falsifier even if its real _delivery_must_fail helper stopped invoking the delivery validator.","horizontal_audit":["negative-helper registration","delivery_validator.validate invocation","credited falsifier semantics","strict learning AST checks","future domain-specific negative helpers"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":20},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-011","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4000314580,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"Heading extraction ignored fenced code but still counted headings hidden inside HTML comments, allowing non-rendered text to impersonate canonical delivery sections.","horizontal_audit":["HTML comment exclusion","rendered Markdown authority","G0-G14 headings","S0-S10 headings","future semantic Markdown parsing"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":21},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-012","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4000314588,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"Heading collection used a set, discarding order and multiplicity. Reordered or duplicated G/S sections could therefore contradict the manifest while governance remained green.","horizontal_audit":["ordered canonical headings","duplicate heading rejection","G0-G14 sequence","S0-S10 sequence","manifest-document consistency"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":22},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-013","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4000404426,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"The strict checker used AST node presence to infer that the delivery negative helper both executed the delivery validator and failed on accepted mutations. Those nodes could be moved under unreachable control flow while static reconciliation still credited the guardrail.","horizontal_audit":["delivery negative helper executable control flow","known-invalid mutation rejection","known-accepted no-op rejection","strict learning runtime probes","future registered negative helpers"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":23},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-014","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4000404430,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"Canonical heading comparison filtered out noncanonical G/S titles before checking multiplicity. A second level-three heading reusing an existing G or S identifier under a shadow title could therefore coexist with the canonical section without being counted as a duplicate semantic identifier.","horizontal_audit":["all level-three G identifiers","all level-three S identifiers","shadow replacement sections","duplicate semantic IDs","roadmap and slice ambiguity"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":24},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-015","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4000404435,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"Heading extraction excluded comments and fenced code but still accepted heading-looking lines inside raw HTML blocks such as script or pre, where Markdown does not render them as semantic sections.","horizontal_audit":["raw HTML container blocks","generic block HTML","script pre style and textarea regions","rendered Markdown headings","future semantic Markdown parsing"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":25},
    {"id":"LEARN-PR152-016","pr":152,"source":"external_review","review_comment_id":4000404440,"class_id":"ADV-GUARDRAIL-ATTESTATION-GAP","invariant_ids":["INV-LEARNING-002"],"root_cause":"The machine-readable execution manifest validated gate IDs, dependencies, E2E flags and authority prerequisites but not each gate name. Planning consumers could therefore see names that contradicted the canonical roadmap while governance remained green.","horizontal_audit":["manifest gate names","G0-G14 canonical mapping","roadmap-to-manifest semantic consistency","AI planning consumers","future gate renames"],"guardrails":[{"path":"tools/assurance/test_validate_d4c_selection.py","probe":"falsify_ai_e2e_delivery_heading_binding"}],"systemic_guardrail_updated":true,"guardrail_generation":26}
